# Review

## Summary

Most technical terms are glossed in place. Information hiding is defined in the opening paragraph. The English account of prompting is paraphrased where it is linked. Spec mining follows a description of the process it names. Relaxing is glossed both as "regaining generality" and as "reverses the earlier code extraction". Constraining is glossed as "narrowing the interpretation space".

The one access problem is order. "Codification" is an active vocabulary term. It first appears unglossed and unlinked in the practical-consequence sentence of "What the interface hides and what leaks". Its gloss and link come one section later. That earlier sentence is the first meaningful mention, so it needs the gloss and link. The two info findings are minor framing gaps that leave each sentence readable.
